      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those smaller, more annoying mishaps are often categorized under broader clauses within the marine insurance policy, though there isn't one single, universally used term for every tiny glitch. Think of them as the low-level, persistent annoyances that are sometimes covered under \"perils of the sea\" or general operational risks. These can range from minor equipment failures on the vessel—like a refrigeration unit sputtering out on refrigerated goods—to minor cargo handling damage during rough seas that aren't severe enough for a major claim. These small issues are precisely what make logistics feel like a constant battle against tiny, unpredictable gremlins.",
